Track 1: The Waterclock Stumbles
- Story & Context: Deep within the sweating greenhouse barracks of La Colmena, Dr. Marcela Vane accidentally jammed a 12-volt hot lead from an overloaded TR-808 circuit into the wet rhizome of a giant Monstera deliciosa. The smell of scorched loam and sweet cellulose instantly filled the control tent as the dying plant triggered a spontaneous, dragging rhythm that locked the sequencer into a sluggish 71 BPM wobble. Refusing to cut the power, Marcela leaned into the smoke and sang through a megaphone while the glass panes rattled in their zinc frames, delivering the line, "the sap is keeping better time than we are." That volatile midnight accident proved biological stress could dictate groove, laying down the blueprint for the entire scene before the dawn could break.
