Track 2: Did You Miss the Solstice Appointment?
- Story & Context: Huddled beside the swollen river at the Puerto Quito ferry depot, Kaelen Ibarra spent fourteen hours shivering in the mist with his modular road-case, waiting for an international courier who never showed. The damp air rusted his toggle switches as he ran patch cables into a flowering night-cereus, capturing its frantic opening pulse to trigger sweeping, celestial filter sweeps across pitch-bent sub-drops. He swallowed cold, bitter guayusa dregs as the town church bells chimed hours late, whispering into the microphone with tired disgust, "we traded the calendar for orbit, so stop checking your wrist." The resulting track captures the bitter isolation of missing every terrestrial deadline while drifting hopelessly in sync with planetary alignments.
